{"tool_name":"genefisher","contents":["oeb","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"genefisher","home":"http://bibiserv.techfak.uni-bielefeld.de/genefisher/","summary":"Interactive primer design tool for standard or degenerate primers; will accept unaligned sequences.","addition_date":"2017-05-01T17:08:59Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:58:57Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:genefisher","credit":[{"email":"robert@techfak.uni-bielefeld.de","name":"R. Giegerich","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://bibiserv.cebitec.uni-bielefeld.de/genefisher2?id=genefisher_manual_manual"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"PCR primer design","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0308"},{"term":"Primer and probe design","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2419"},{"term":"Primer removal","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3237"}]}],"name":"Genefisher","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"metadata":{"abstract":"When a family of genes from closely related organisms is known, there is a certain change to extract the corresponding gene from the genome of another related organism. This can be done by polymerase chain reaction, provided that a pair of suitable primers can be designed. In contrast to primer design for a single, known target sequence, systematic primer design for an unknown target given a group of homologues can by no means be done manually. GeneFisher is a software tool which automates this task, and takes special care to make the impact of the manifold design parameters transparent to the user.","authors":[{"name":"Giegerich R."},{"name":"Meyer F."},{"name":"Schleiermacher C."}],"citationCount":149,"date":"1996-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Proceedings / ... International Conference on Intelligent Systems for Molecular Biology ; ISMB. International Conference on Intel